Veeam is the Data and AI Trust Company, specializing in helping organizations ensure their data and AI are fully understood, secured, and resilient to enable the acceleration of safe AI at scale. As the market leader in both data resilience and data security posture management, Veeam is built for the convergence of identity, data, security, and AI risk. Headquartered in Seattle with offices in more than 30 countries, Veeam protects over 550,000 customers worldwide, who trust Veeam to keep their businesses running. Join us as we go fearlessly forward together, growing, learning, and making a real impact for some of the world’s biggest brands.

About the role:

The Sales Engineer partners with the Sales Team to break down technical barriers to sales, acting as the technical advisor for customers, partners and resellers. &nbsp;

You will present Veeam messaging to audiences of varying size and seniority, including CXOs, chief architects and IT management. You will create content and deliver demonstrations that support this messaging, in conjunction with Channel Partners. The role also includes channel training, so that partners can independently position and resell Veeam to their customers. The successful candidate is a self-motivated, technically competent Veeam presales engineer with a track record of partnering with other groups in the sales and support organisation to close sales. The role requires strength and a background in defining architectural strategies that guide customers toward the adoption of Veeam technologies. &nbsp;

This is a primarily customer-focused, field-based technical role. You will work closely with the field sales and channel teams to inform and energise partners, resellers and end users about our product offerings. The role is as much about being an evangelist for Veeam as being a great technical resource. &nbsp;

The Sales Engineer acts in a consultative fashion and is looked to as the expert in all of the products by sales, channel and other sales engineers. The role calls for a highly autonomous, self-driven approach and the ability to influence people at all levels, both internally and externally. &nbsp;

What You'll Do:

• Perform live customer meeting presentations and demonstrations &nbsp;

• Implement and manage POCs through to technical closure &nbsp;

• Generate leads through activities such as events, webinars and user groups &nbsp;

• Understand and negotiate technical requirements with customers and partners &nbsp;

• Engage actively with the virtualisation community (strongly encouraged) &nbsp;

• Perform online demonstrations &nbsp;

• Working closely with the sales department to secure new partners and customers &nbsp;

• Work closely with the development department to relay customer feedback &nbsp;

• Providing pre-sales support as they evaluate Veeam software &nbsp;

What You'll Bring

• Bachelor’s degree (or a combination of education and experience will be considered) &nbsp;

• Five or more years of solution sales experience &nbsp;

• Experience with Data Protection is a plus &nbsp;

• Demonstrated experience with virtualisation technologies &nbsp;

• Experience in data life cycle management with IT audit requirements &nbsp;

• Strong presentation skills &nbsp;

• Excellent verbal and written communication skills; must be able to present to groups &nbsp;

• Self-starter who is high-energy and motivated, able to work independently with limited direction in a fast-paced environment and to learn new technologies quickly &nbsp;

• Ability to adapt to changes in roles and responsibilities &nbsp;

• Ability to travel within the region as required &nbsp;

